      "summary": "An archaeological survey sampled n sites uniformly without replacement from a finite set of N sites and found zero sites containing an artifact. If K sites in the full set contained artifacts, the exact probability of seeing zero was C(N-K,n)/C(N,n). To form a one-sided 95% upper bound on K, analysts found the largest K for which that zero-result probability remained at least 0.05, then compared K/N with the required ceiling.",
